## Remount Secure provides enhanced security via mount options:
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Security-misc#Remount_Secure
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Noexec

## Enabled by default at level 3 (nosuid, nodev and noexec for all mount points,
## including /home).

## The level is NOT configured on the kernel command line. Configure it with a
## drop-in file instead:
##   /etc/remount-secure.d/*.conf           (admin)
##   /usr/local/etc/remount-secure.d/*.conf (local admin, highest precedence)
## containing, for example:
##   remount_secure_level=2
## or use the helper:
##   sudo remount-secure --set-level 2
## Levels: 0 = off; 1 = nosuid,nodev; 2 = + noexec except /home;
##         3 = + noexec including /home.

## Debugging only: add 'noremountsecure' to the kernel command line to disable
## remount-secure for a single boot (e.g. to recover from an exec-related boot
## problem). This does not change the configured level.
